<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 57 0 R
/E (Every hospital must keep track of who the patients are, which doctors are available and who should be treated next. When this is done on paper, records are lost, the same patient is registered twice and urgent cases may wait behind routine ones. A computerized system reduces these problems and saves the time of both staff and patients.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
95 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 57 0 R
/E (This project demonstrates the idea on a small scale. The receptionist registers a patient using a form. The browser \(frontend\) sends the details to the Java backend using a REST request. The backend validates and normalizes the input, stores the patient in a HashMap and, if required, places the patient in the waiting queue according to the severity of the case. When the doctor is free, the next patient is called from the front of the queue and the details are shown on the page.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
